  "decisions": [
    "Five visible columns: fish, catch location, water/catch type, minimum skill, no-fail skill. Cooking and bonuses remain deferred.",
    "Every item identity was rechecked against the current Wowhead Forever tooltip. Classic guides corroborate all 22 Classic fish habitats; Whimsyfin uses a current Forever community guide.",
    "Classic skill bands remain references; exact Forever thresholds are unverified. The mid/high cast minimums have an independent Classic guide, while low-zone no-fail values use negative Classic bases plus 95.",
    "The Classic leveling guide incorrectly collapses all low zones into a 1/96 band; it is not used for starter/capital no-fail values. ForeverDB and Forever Changes distinguish 25 and 75, and the Forever beta guide supports 75 in capitals.",
    "Forever Changes gives chance-only minima 51/126/201/326, whereas inspected Classic success/cast logic and the independent Classic cast guide support 55/130/205/330. Neither proves exact Forever thresholds.",
    "Classic code contains extra hard-coded cast gates including Stormwind and Wailing Caverns that disagree with the guides. Retained low-zone values are references, not server verification.",
    "Public Fishing Bobber records corroborate a catch in Forever, sometimes with a representative zone. Aggregated counts are not claimed as per-coordinate counts.",
    "Riverglades was searched through public guides, search results, zone data, and current Trout/Greater Sagefish source records. No independent catch/habitat/skill verification was obtained. Missing evidence is not evidence of absence.",
    "Whimsyfin minimum 55 was an unsupported inference from ordinary Redridge water and is removed. Approximately 150 no-fail is retained as a community report.",
    "Longjaw Mud Snapper in Loch Modan is restored after the detailed Classic loot guide corroborated it; the partial snapshot catch list did not establish absence.",
    "Raw Sagefish uses named freshwater schools. Greater Sagefish uses freshwater schools in Alterac/Stranglethorn; Stranglethorn also has a current Forever catch record.",
    "Glossy Mightfish in Feralas coastal water is corroborated by the independent Classic guide, although a snapshot reference comment mentions an unlinked reference. The exact Forgotten Coast label is generalized to Feralas coast.",
    "Nightfin/Sunscale server-time windows and Winter Squid/Summer Bass dates are explicit Classic guide references, not verified Forever restrictions.",
    "Unknown or missing water/source labels display Unverified or a reference fallback and cannot block loading. Quest progress is not changed."
  ],
